        "urduTitle": "تعارف",
        "text": "nimals have really two environments: an external environment in which the organism is situated, and an internal environment in which the tissue of the body live. The external environment consists of varying conditions of environment. The internal environment is formed by the circulating organic liquid called lymph or plasma which surrounds and bathes all the tissues. Homeostasis is the tendency of an organism or cell to regulate its internal conditions, such as the chemical composition of its body fluids, so as to maintain health and functioning, regardless of outside conditions. The organism or cell maintains homeostasis by monitoring its internal conditions and responding appropriately when these conditions deviate from their normal state.",
