        "headingUrdu": "نشووند میں نیوکلس کا کردار",
        "headingPashto": "په نشووند کې دنیوکلیس رول",
        "urduTitle": "نشووند میں نیوکلس کا کردار",
        "text": "Importance of nucleus in development was expressed in a unicellular alga, the Acetabularia. It is 2 to 3 inches in length, inhabits European seawater. It has a stalk with a characteristic cap and base containing nucleus. The two species of this alga are different in the shape of their cap.\n\nThe plants develop hats with features of both species. Wha! controls development of the hats the nucleus or chemicals in the cytoplasm?\n\nin Acetabularia If the intermediate hats are removed, new ones grow that correspond to the nucleus in the rhizoid. What does this suggest about the role of the nucleus and chemical messengers in the development of the cell?\n\nand vice versa. A whole new alga forms from the jointed pieces. It was found that the new caps regenerated according to the type of nucleus present in the base. The nucleus exerts a strong influence on the development of cap through the messenger RNA. This is the evidence for nuclear control in developmental process.",
