        "text": "Gregor Mendel's \"hereditary factors\" were purely an abstract concept when he proposed their existence in 1865. At that time, no cellular structures were known that could house for these imaginary units. Today we can show that genes - Mendel's \"factors\" are located along chromosome and we can see the locations of a particular gene by tagging chromosome with a florescent dye that highlights that gene.",
