        "urduTitle": "کروموسوموں کی تعداد",
        "text": "The number of chromosome varies from species to specics and usually it is a characteristic feature of many species. Penicillium, a fungus, has only one pair of chromosome, while some ferns have more than 500 pairs. Many species have two sets of chromosomes in their somatic cells, hence called diploid, while some may have more than two sets of chromosomes; they are called polyploids (tetraploid, hexaploid). The term \"haploid\" is referred to the number of chromosome exactly half than the somatic number of chromosome. Gametes and spores are usually haploid cells. A haploid cell may be monoploid (one set), diploid (two sets), triploid (three sets), and etc.\n\n46(2n) 42 (61)\n\nHaploid Monoploid (n)\n\n23(n)\n\n21(3m)",
