        "headingPashto": "دجين ترکیب",
        "urduTitle": "جین کی ساخت",
        "text": "We have already discussed that a gene is a particular segment of DNA in which nucleotide sequence determines the sequence of amino acid of a polypeptide. A gene usually has regulatory regions and a structural region. The regulatory region located to the 5' end of coding strand of the gene is called promoter that controls the binding RNA polymerase during transcription. Other regulatory region, the terminator, is located to the 3' end of coding strand of the gene. The terminator region causes RNA polymerase to stop transcription. The region between promoter and terminator is structural region of the gene that comprises information (genetic code) for a particular polypeptide or functional RNA. In eukaryotic genes the information of structural region is interrupted by the non-functional sequences called introns whereas the functional sequences are called exons. There is no such pattern of introns and exons in prokaryotic DNA. In prokaryotes many adjacent structural gene that synthesize different polypeptides are regulated by same promoter and terminator regions. Such a group of genes is called operon.",
